{"id":32596,"date":"2025-08-07T17:45:57","date_gmt":"2025-08-07T21:45:57","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/?page_id=32596"},"modified":"2025-10-14T13:19:31","modified_gmt":"2025-10-14T17:19:31","slug":"apd-evaluations","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/apd-evaluations\/","title":{"rendered":"APD Evaluations"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text is-stacked-on-mobile is-vertically-aligned-center auditory-processing-image-1\"><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"516\" height=\"625\" src=\"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/auditoryprocessingdisorderguidebyelevateaudiologydocument1.avif\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-32644 size-full\"\/><\/figure><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center\">Elevate Audiology\u2019s<br>\u201cAuditory Processing Disorder Guide\u201d<\/h2>\n<\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p>Are you interested in learning more about APD? Request a complimentary copy of our Auditory Processing Disorder Guide by Dr. Katelyn Ooms by filling out the form below.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<iframe\n\n    src=\" https:\/\/system.elevateaudiology.com\/widget\/form\/RKvRDMWuUNpjx11JEY6i\"\n\n    style=\"width:100%;height:100%;border:none;border-radius:3px\"\n\n    id=\"inline-RKvRDMWuUNpjx11JEY6i\"\n\n    data-layout=\"{'id':'INLINE'}\"\n\n    data-trigger-type=\"alwaysShow\"\n\n    data-trigger-value=\"\"\n\n    data-activation-type=\"alwaysActivated\"\n\n    data-activation-value=\"\"\n\n    data-deactivation-type=\"neverDeactivate\"\n\n    data-deactivation-value=\"\"\n\n    data-form-name=\"APD Report Opt In Form\"\n\n    data-height=\"884\"\n\n    data-layout-iframe-id=\"inline-RKvRDMWuUNpjx11JEY6i\"\n\n    data-form-id=\"RKvRDMWuUNpjx11JEY6i\"\n\n    title=\"APD Report Opt In Form\"\n\n>\n\n<\/iframe>\n\n<script src=\" https:\/\/system.elevateaudiology.com\/js\/form_embed.js%22%3e%3c\/script\"><\/script>\n\n\n\n<p>Our clinic offers comprehensive auditory processing evaluations customized to each individual\u2019s age, concerns and communication needs. Since no two cases of Auditory Processing Disorder (APD) are exactly alike, we conduct a thorough hearing evaluation followed by a carefully selected battery of 6 to 9 evidence-based tests. These assessments help us pinpoint specific areas of auditory breakdown and create a detailed profile of both strengths and challenges, guiding accurate diagnosis and targeted intervention.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\"><div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"602\" height=\"1070\" src=\"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/testing11.avif\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-32599\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1;object-fit:contain\" srcset=\"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/testing11.avif 602w, https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/testing11-600x1066.jpg 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 602px) 100vw, 602px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\"><div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"602\" height=\"1071\" src=\"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/testing2apd1.avif\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-32600\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1;object-fit:contain\" srcset=\"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/testing2apd1.avif 602w, https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/testing2apd1-600x1067.jpg 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 602px) 100vw, 602px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<p>The evaluation process begins with a thorough case history, questionnaires and baseline audiological testing to rule out hearing loss. Based on age, cognitive level and presenting symptoms, we select a customized set of assessments that may include tests of:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Auditory attention<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Sound discrimination<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Binaural integration and separation<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Auditory closure<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Auditory pattern recognition<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p>These tests allow us to evaluate how the brain processes different types of auditory information in various listening conditions.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>After testing, our team compiles a comprehensive report outlining diagnostic impressions, clinical observations and personalized recommendations. These may include therapy options, classroom or workplace accommodations and strategies for home or school.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Our goal is to provide clear answers and practical solutions\u2014empowering individuals with APD to strengthen their listening skills, boost communication confidence and thrive in everyday environments.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Here\u2019s a link to our FAQ page, where you can find clear answers to common questions about our APD program and what to expect: <a href=\"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/auditory-processing-disorder-apd-faq\/\">Click here<\/a>.<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Call Elevate Audiology at <a href=\"tel:(864) 447-6611\">(864) 447-6611<\/a> for the Easley office or <a href=\"tel:(864) 447-4183\">(864) 447-4183<\/a> for the Greenville office for more information or to schedule an appointment.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Elevate Audiology\u2019s\u201cAuditory Processing Disorder Guide\u201d Are you interested in learning more about APD? Request a complimentary copy of our Auditory Processing Disorder Guide by Dr. Katelyn Ooms by filling out the form below. Our clinic offers comprehensive auditory processing evaluations customized to each individ